{"id": "EUVD-2026-101229", "enisaUuid": "be4f7573-01cf-3731-ae33-79fe2ac9caa9", "description": "libsixel before 1.8.7-r1 and 1.9.0 through 1.10.5 contains a heap out-of-bounds write vulnerability in gif_init_frame() in src/fromgif.c, which never checks the GIF transparent color index against the palette size. Attackers can supply a crafted GIF with a small color table and large transparent index, processed with a background color set, to write bytes past the palette buffer, causing heap corruption or crashes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T01:04:11", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/saitoha/libsixel/issues/220", "https://github.com/saitoha/libsixel/commit/bdbab09816eb9188429c37a50b97c5e66dfe5047", "https://github.com/saitoha/libsixel/releases/tag/v1.8.7-r1", "https://github.com/saitoha/libsixel/blob/v1.8.7/src/fromgif.c#L182-L248", "https://github.com/libsixel/libsixel/blob/v1.10.5/src/fromgif.c#L219-L240", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libsixel-gif-transparent-index-oob-write", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libsixel-before-1.8.7-r1-and-1.9.0-through-1.10.5-heap-out-of-bounds-write-via-gif"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5j3r-7cc6-965h", "CVE-2026-110601"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19d962a3-d49b-3b00-946d-20d3cd76a9cf", "product": {"name": "libsixel", "vendor": {"name": "saitoha"}}, "product_version": "1.9.0 \u22641.10.5"}, {"id": "3ff2f621-e765-31c0-81c1-48a62be14021", "product": {"name": "libsixel", "vendor": {"name": "saitoha"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.8.7-r1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "983f99f9-751b-3ce3-9161-e1d80c82f5f7", "vendor": {"name": "saitoha"}}], "isExploited": false}